--TEST--
a promoted constructor parameter's visibility keyword is the property's own, so a `private` one is refused outside its class and a `protected` one outside the chain — `rule:classes/promotion-is-constructor-only`, `rule:core-api/written-visibility`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The keyword that promotes is the keyword the access check reads:
// `nvs_types::signatures` records the level beside the property's type, so a
// promoted parameter reaches the same check a written declaration does and
// needs no case of its own.
class Vault {
    public function constructor(private string $secret, protected string $note, public string $label) {}
    public function reveal(): string {
        // Inside the declaring class every level is reachable.
        return $this->secret;
    }
}

class Branch extends Vault {
    public function seen(): string {
        // `protected` reaches down the `extends` chain, so this is accepted
        // and the refusals below are about where the access is written.
        return $this->note;
    }
}

Vault $v = new Vault("shh", "seen", "front");
echo $v->label, "\n";
echo $v->secret, "\n";
echo $v->note, "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0471]: `Vault::$secret` is `private`, so only `Vault`'s own bodies reach it
%A
error[E0471]: `Vault::$note` is `protected`, so only `Vault` and the classes that extend it reach it
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
